course: dictionary
lesson: 5521
title: Who is a learner?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A learner is a person who is learning something. A pupil in class is a learner, and so is someone learning a new skill, like swimming or chess.
explain: Read the clues in the sentence: «Curiosity is how we learn: asking "why?" and then looking for the answer yourself makes you a strong learner.» A strong learner is someone who is good at learning, so it is a good thing to be.
explain: A learner driver is someone learning to drive who has not passed the driving test yet. In the UK and Ireland, a red L on a white plate, called an L-plate, tells other drivers that a learner is at the wheel, so they should be patient. «A learner driver has L plates and a grown-up beside them.»
fact: A learner is a person who is learning something.
fact: «A fast learner» picks things up quickly. «A slow learner» needs more time to get things.
fact: A learner driver has not passed the driving test yet.
fact: An L-plate is a red L on a white background, used in the UK and Ireland.
fact: Pinyin writes Chinese sounds with Latin letters and tone marks, and it helps learners with pronunciation.
exercise: «Curiosity is how we learn.» What is a learner? | *A person who is learning something | A teacher who gives tests | A car with a red L | Someone who has finished school forever
exercise: What does an L-plate show? | The car is a school bus | *A learner is driving the car | The road is closed | A car is for sale
exercise: «He is a fast learner.» What does fast learner mean? | *Someone who picks things up quickly | Someone who runs very fast in races | Someone who lives far away | Someone who cannot learn at all
test: A learner driver has not yet passed what? | A spelling test | A maths test | A swimming test | *The driving test
test: «Saying Je ne comprends pas is smart, not silly: every language learner needs it.» What is a language learner? | A person who never goes to school | A person who can already speak every language | A teacher of French | *A person learning a new language
exam: Which one is NOT a learner? | Someone learning to swim | A child learning to read | *A driver who has already passed the driving test | A pupil in a classroom
